        "body": "## Description\n\nThere is a race condition in the merge logic. Merging cell results in `defer` mode results in out-of-order rendering. The immediate reason for it is `siblingIndex` being `undefined` in `attachWidget()` method:\n\nhttps://github.com/jupyterlab/jupyterlab/blob/cf5029786133fac829dc094d5f5de16fa1cda729/packages/notebook/src/windowing.ts#L403-L411\n\n## Reproduce\n\nBefore merge (note that it has to be selected from bottom to the top)\n\n<img width=\"1073\" height=\"600\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5ca5fafa-ba28-4929-a8ae-001ee9b0ea55\" />\n\nAfter merge\n\n<img width=\"1073\" height=\"493\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1bd49ab7-d00b-45ee-8443-fd2c72f86e9a\" />\n\nincorrect `windowing-list-index`\n\n<img width=\"1605\" height=\"112\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/126ec855-5b68-4105-915e-128751c55c09\" />\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nCells render in the correct order.\n\n## Context\n\nThis does not appear to happen in `none`, `contentVisibility`, nor `full` windowing modes 🤔 \n\n- Browser and version: Chrome and Edge\n- JupyterLab version: 4.5.0",
